# Access to {{ calls_domain }} for your AI agent

Give this file to your agent. It holds an API key: keep it as private as a
password, and delete the key in trip2g's admin (API keys) to revoke it.

- Instance: https://{{ calls_domain }}
- API key: `{{ calls_secrets.AGENT_API_KEY }}`
- GraphQL: https://{{ calls_domain }}/graphql (header `X-API-Key`)
- MCP: https://{{ calls_domain }}/_system/mcp (header `X-API-Key`)

## Read and search the vault over MCP

Claude Code:

```sh
claude mcp add --transport http calls https://{{ calls_domain }}/_system/mcp --header "X-API-Key: {{ calls_secrets.AGENT_API_KEY }}"
```

Any other MCP client: a streamable HTTP server at the URL above with the
header `X-API-Key: {{ calls_secrets.AGENT_API_KEY }}`.

## Sync a folder of notes

```sh
curl -fsSLo trip2g-sync.mjs https://raw.githubusercontent.com/trip2g/trip2g/{{ trip2g_sync_ref }}/onboarding-vault/.obsidian/plugins/trip2g/trip2g-sync.mjs
export TRIP2G_API_KEY={{ calls_secrets.AGENT_API_KEY }}
node trip2g-sync.mjs --api-url https://{{ calls_domain }}/graphql --dry-run <folder>
node trip2g-sync.mjs --api-url https://{{ calls_domain }}/graphql <folder>
```

The first command shows what would be pushed; the second pushes it. Add
`--two-way` to also pull the notes that changed on the server. Deleting a
synced file and syncing again hides that note on the server.
